# Notices and acknowledgements

SwiftLSL contains no code from any other project. It has no dependencies outside the
Swift standard library and Apple's system frameworks; `lsltool`, a development harness
rather than a shipped product, additionally uses `apple/swift-argument-parser` (MIT).

## Lab Streaming Layer

SwiftLSL implements the LSL wire protocol, inlet side. The protocol was reconstructed
from the public documentation and from reading the reference implementation,
[`sccn/liblsl`](https://github.com/sccn/liblsl) (MIT, © 2012 Christian A. Kothe), at
commit `e651023`. What was taken is protocol facts — field names, byte layouts, magic
constants, formulas — recorded with `file:line` citations throughout
[SCOPE.md](SCOPE.md) §2. No liblsl source was copied or transliterated.

Two areas sit closer to expression than to fact and were handled deliberately
(SCOPE.md §10):

- The **test-pattern generator** (`src/sample.cpp:356-405`) produces values that are
  protocol constants and must match byte for byte, but `Sources/LSLCore/TestPattern.swift`
  was written from the specification in SCOPE.md §2.2, not from the C++.
- The **RLS dejitterer** (`src/time_postprocessor.cpp:104-131`) is out of scope
  (SCOPE.md §9) and is not present here. Porting it later would mean porting
  expression, and would carry liblsl's MIT notice with it.

